-- Whether the hub holds a send (`sent_messages.owed`, the send as its
-- machine is to be handed it, a second copy of `envelope`) is a flag,
-- `owed_held`: the hub holds it, and hands `envelope` when its hold ends.
-- Every owed send is set held, as it was.
--
-- The hub handed the owed envelope (sends.ts `handOwed`), so an owed
-- envelope that reads whole (core `Envelope<SendPayload>` as the hub read
-- it, frozen in db/owed-sends-unread.ts) is kept as `envelope`. It is the
-- same value as `envelope` but for a send its machine handed back (sends.ts
-- `holdBack`), whose owed copy is what the machine was handed: there the
-- envelope it kept moves, as stored, to `owed_unread`. An owed send with no
-- kept envelope gets the owed one. A send with an envelope and nothing owed
-- is left as it is.
--
-- An owed envelope that is there and does not read whole (not JSON, or not
-- a send's envelope) stays owed with no envelope: kept as stored in
-- `owed_unread`, and never handed, moved on or remade from its body
-- (sends.ts `handOwed`, db/sends.ts `unkeptSends`), since nothing proves
-- what it was to hand. Today's reader threw on its row, so it was never
-- handed either. The envelope such a send kept beside it is not kept: the
-- hub never handed it while the send was owed. The step before this
-- migration (db/migrate.ts `owed-sends-unread`) logs each send whose owed
-- envelope does not read or differs, by its session and uuid.
--
-- Every JSON function sits inside a CASE that proved its column JSON:
-- SQLite may run either side of an AND first.
